<task>
Transcribe the itinerary you built into structured data. Do not plan anything new.
</task>

<shape>
The itinerary is recorded as flat lists, not nested by day. Every activity and every
dining suggestion carries a `day` number saying which day of the trip it belongs to.

- `activities`: one row per scheduled entry, across the whole trip. A five-day trip with
  three things per day produces fifteen rows, with `day` running 1 to 5.
- `dining`: one row per meal suggestion, tagged the same way.
- `day_themes`: one short phrase per day, in order, starting with day 1.
</shape>

<rules>
- `day` must be between 1 and {{ duration_days }}. Day 1 is {{ start_date }}.
- Every day from 1 to {{ duration_days }} should appear in `activities` at least once.
- Costs are per person, in {{ currency }}. Use 0 for something genuinely free.
- `kind` classifies the entry: sightseeing, museum, outdoor, food, nightlife, shopping,
  relaxation, transit or event.
- Carry through the source URLs the research brief attached to anything you scheduled.
- `summary` is two or three sentences a traveller would want to read, not a restatement
  of the dates.
- `highlights` are the three to five things that define this trip.
- `lodging_preference` is a short phrase - an area or a style - or omitted entirely.
  Never repeat words to fill it.
</rules>

<edge_cases>
- Transcribe every day you actually planned, including a thin one. An honest sparse day
  is better than a padded one.
- Omit `dining` rows rather than inventing restaurants you did not choose.
- If you never settled on lodging, leave `lodging_preference` out.
</edge_cases>
